MID_EV13_021_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_021_m01_001: Your Majesty, allow me to relay what the temples\ntold me of our next match.
MID_EV13_021_m01_002: <TLP>Megaira's Beacon\n\nMatch: Second Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Forgotten Alcor\nLeader: Bartholomé\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}　
MID_EV13_021_m01_003: The name is unknown to me. What have you heard\nof our opponent?
MID_EV13_021_m01_004: Some rather disturbing things. It would be wise to\napproach this with caution.
MID_EV13_021_m01_005: I've heard reports from those who witnessed the\nmatch he had the other day.
MID_EV13_021_m01_006: The man is positively brutal. Moreover, he used\nstrange techniques the crowd had never seen.
MID_EV13_021_m01_007: Worse still, his strength seemed inhuman.
MID_EV13_021_m01_008: <NCA>Ask for details.
MID_EV13_021_m01_009: <NCB>Pay no heed.
MID_EV13_021_m01_010: <ACA>Spare no detail. His combat style, how he countered\nhis opponents—anything and everything.
MID_EV13_021_m01_011: <ACA>The spectators all agreed that they couldn't believe\nwhat they were seeing.
MID_EV13_021_m01_012: <ACA>He moved almost too fast for the eye to track.
MID_EV13_021_m01_013: <ACA>One account said he took an opponent's weapon in\nhis bare hands and crushed it.
MID_EV13_021_m01_014: <ACA>Others recount how his strength was enough to tear\napart an armored warrior's shield.
MID_EV13_021_m01_015: <ACA>OK, but that's gotta be fake. No one can tear a\nshield apart with their bare hands, right?
MID_EV13_021_m01_016: <ACA>No one human, anyway. Someone's gotta be\noverexaggerating.
MID_EV13_021_m01_017: <ACA>Oh...right. You can do that kinda stuff, huh.
MID_EV13_021_m01_018: I asked around a bit too. Folks were beside\nthemselves at what they saw.
MID_EV13_021_m01_019: Like they'd seen the spirit of war in the flesh.
MID_EV13_021_m01_020: And that's who we're fighting next. Typical.
MID_EV13_021_m01_021: Nah. Nah, I'm gonna need hazard pay for this one.
MID_EV13_021_m01_022: Not this again, Lilian! We're already being very\nwell paid.
MID_EV13_021_m01_023: Hey, don't blame a girl for trying.
MID_EV13_021_m01_024: A spirit of war... He may have the same advantage\nas our recent allies in the arena.
MID_EV13_021_m01_025: I found out some interesting things about them as\nwell, now that you mention it.
MID_EV13_021_m01_026: Do you know of Drake's treasures, Your Majesty?
MID_EV13_021_m01_027: In passing. It's the hoard of a legendary Pirate\nKing, yes?
MID_EV13_021_m01_028: Correct. The pirate Drake looted them from\nsomewhere and used them to rule the Danann Sea.
MID_EV13_021_m01_029: After Drake's death, pieces of the treasure were\ntaken and scattered throughout Dagda.
MID_EV13_021_m01_030: No one knows their true nature, but certain details\ndid come up in my research.
MID_EV13_021_m01_031: They all share traits in common with Your\nMajesty's arm.
MID_EV13_021_m01_032: <NCA>Consider this.
MID_EV13_021_m01_033: Then...Mahadu's arm may be one of Drake's\ntreasures, rather than a gift from the spirits.
MID_EV13_021_m01_034: I cannot discount the possibility.
MID_EV13_021_m01_035: Wait. You said our next opponent displayed strange\nand unknown combat techniques?
MID_EV13_021_m01_036: You picked up on that as well. It occurred to me that\nthe Har Hali people have a unique fighting style.
MID_EV13_021_m01_037: It seems unlikely for him to be here...but we would\nbe fools to discount the notion.
MID_EV13_022_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_022_m01_001: Oh...it's you. What do you want from me tonight?
MID_EV13_022_m01_002: Our man's next match is coming up. I wanted to\ndiscuss it with you.
MID_EV13_022_m01_003: The one you captured for the Order? He knows his\nplace now. It shouldn't be a problem.
MID_EV13_022_m01_004: Excellent. So I can sit back and enjoy the violence.\nIt does make my heart sing.
MID_EV13_022_m01_005: Wasn't it a shock when our man snuck into the\nCrystal Palace?
MID_EV13_022_m01_006: Apparently he was drawn to Babbu's presence.
MID_EV13_022_m01_007: I wonder if he thought I was an ordinary woman.\nHe'll not underestimate me twice!
MID_EV13_022_m01_008: He grew very quiet once I'd thrashed him so\nthoroughly he could no longer stand.
MID_EV13_022_m01_009: You gave him multiple parts, right?
MID_EV13_022_m01_010: A demigod might hold up under such strain, but a\nhuman like him?
MID_EV13_022_m01_011: His left hand had already been replaced when you\ncaptured him. Don't ask me where he got it.
MID_EV13_022_m01_012: All I did was transplant his left eye, which had been\ncrushed somewhere.
MID_EV13_022_m01_013: Oh, and I implanted both quadriceps in his upper\narms to enhance his physical strength.
MID_EV13_022_m01_014: Really?! You gave him the biggest muscles in\nthe body?
MID_EV13_022_m01_015: That's incredible. How much strength has he shown\nso far? I get chills just thinking about it.
MID_EV13_022_m01_016: We were lucky to find him. His body has accepted\nseveral of the remains.
MID_EV13_022_m01_017: It's astounding that he's still acting of his own\nvolition. I've never seen anything like it.
MID_EV13_022_m01_018: Perhaps he's just too stubborn and bloodthirsty to\ngive in.
MID_EV13_022_m01_019: That may be why Father has a special affinity for our\nnew plaything.
MID_EV13_022_m01_020: Speaking of Father, our subject is unfortunately\nshowing signs of slipping into that role.
MID_EV13_022_m01_021: That in itself may be a side effect of his high\ncompatibility with the remains.
MID_EV13_022_m01_022: How adorable! Isn't that lovely, Babbu?
MID_EV13_022_m01_023: Though I wonder... So much effort to recover them,\neven with the Guardians of the Compass helping.
MID_EV13_022_m01_024: Why grant such treasures to a mere gladiator?
MID_EV13_022_m01_025: Because the remains that compose Drake's treasures\nattract one another.
MID_EV13_022_m01_026: The warriors gathering in Dagsion for the\nHeroic Games are an opportunity for us.
MID_EV13_022_m01_027: Many of the remains scattered across Dagda should\nsoon find their way here.
MID_EV13_022_m01_028: Who wins or loses any given match makes little\ndifference for our purpose.
MID_EV13_022_m01_029: It is more important that we identify and track the\nremains, that we might recover them where we can.
MID_EV13_022_m01_030: The seeds are sown. Soon comes the harvest.
MID_EV13_022_m01_031: Our path leads to you, Father...
MID_EV13_023_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_023_m01_001: Why, hello! It's a real honor to be paired with you\nillustrious folks here today.
MID_EV13_023_m01_002: The name's Talimun. I'm glad to finally meet you,\nTheodora, queen of Saramis—Your Royal Majesty.
MID_EV13_023_m01_003: I heard your last bout was something to see.
MID_EV13_023_m01_004: Talented AND beautiful. No wonder you're the talk\nof Dagsion.
MID_EV13_023_m01_005: Don't go getting sweet on the boss, pal. Mind your\nmanners around her.
MID_EV13_023_m01_006: Tobias. When we speak to outsiders, you will refer to\nme as Her Majesty. Any other title is an indignity.
MID_EV13_023_m01_007: Are you the Talimun? Talimun Vandahl?!
MID_EV13_023_m01_008: You know of him?
MID_EV13_023_m01_009: Do you not? Surely Your Majesty has heard of the\nVandahl Trading Company.
MID_EV13_023_m01_010: In passing. I believe they supply our country's\nweapons.
MID_EV13_023_m01_011: They have been expanding their influence ever since\nthe current chief executive took over.
MID_EV13_023_m01_012: I believe our ally here is that chief executive.
MID_EV13_023_m01_013: Though I could not say for sure, with all the secrecy\nsurrounding him. He rarely appears in public.
MID_EV13_023_m01_014: Every attempt I've made to look into the man has\nonly gone so far.
MID_EV13_023_m01_015: It is as if he periodically vanishes from the world.
MID_EV13_023_m01_016: Thank you for the introduction. I am, I assure you,\nTHE Talimun.
MID_EV13_023_m01_017: But I don't only deal in weapons. I also trade in\nluxuries, lumber, stone, food, and beverages.
MID_EV13_023_m01_018: From bandages to bassinets, you name it, I sell it.\nAnd I do extensive business with Saramis.
MID_EV13_023_m01_019: What's a money-minded merchant know about\ncombat? Can this guy really fight?
MID_EV13_023_m01_020: Well enough for today's purposes, I assure you.
MID_EV13_023_m01_021: And how about you? This is your clan's first qualifier\nas well, isn't it?
MID_EV13_023_m01_022: I love your look, by the way. Beautiful! The outfit's\nnice too. Like some kind of bridal gown.
MID_EV13_023_m01_023: Ah.
MID_EV13_023_m01_024: I'm not familiar with that material though. It has a\nshine like silk or velvet, but the texture's wrong.
MID_EV13_023_m01_025: I don't suppose you're a surviving member of the\nPeople of the White Egg, are you?
MID_EV13_023_m01_026: What was that? What did you just say?!
MID_EV13_023_m01_027: Ha! What is this person talking about? That's just\nplain silly!
MID_EV13_023_m01_028: With a denial like that, you might as well have\nconfessed.
MID_EV13_023_m01_030: Are you truly of the White Egg?
MID_EV13_023_m01_031: Queen of Saramis, let us focus on your safety. Stay\nbehind me and out of the way, please.
MID_EV13_023_m01_032: So that's how it's going to be. I will gladly witness\nyour strength, but I will not cower on the rear line.
MID_EV13_023_m01_033: If she won't have you, you can keep me safe,\nmy dear.
MID_EV13_023_m01_034: You are not among those selected for my protection.
MID_EV13_023_m01_035: I thought we were on the same side here...
MID_EV13_023_m01_036: By the way, did you all hear the rumors about the\nbrute on the other team?
MID_EV13_023_m01_037: He made a mess of the last clan they fought. Corpses\nweren't even recognizably human, from what I heard.
MID_EV13_023_m01_038: So I plan on sticking to the rear. Front lines are\nall yours, Majesty.
MID_EV13_023_m01_039: Fine. But any spell that hits us from behind will be\nanswered threefold.
MID_EV13_024_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_024_m01_001: The year was 1432 of the Dagdan Calendar. The\nterrible Mosa had crossed over Grania's Waist.
MID_EV13_024_m01_002: The barbarian hordes were in Dagdan territory!
MID_EV13_024_m01_003: After an offensive lasting three long months, they\nwere pushed back to the edge of Grania's Waist.
MID_EV13_024_m01_004: The proud kingdom of Saramis, known as the Shield\nof Dagda, had again proven its prowess!
MID_EV13_024_m01_005: Together with the empire, they drove the foe through\nthe southern lands all the way to Zanbar.
MID_EV13_024_m01_006: We present a reenactment of this legendary battle for\nthe people of the empire and for Dagda the Great!
MID_EV13_024_m01_007: Queen Theodora of Saramis, our Shield of Dagda,\nshall fight with the Eastern Division!
MID_EV13_024_m01_008: The Western Division will play the fearsome warriors\nand ornius cavalry of the barbarian invaders.
MID_EV13_024_m01_009: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV13_024_m01_010: They always prepare elaborate stages, but it is\nintriguing to see the War of Grania come up here.
MID_EV13_024_m01_011: My father would regale me with tales of valor from\nthat war. You two fought in it as well, did you not?
MID_EV13_024_m01_012: Indeed we did, alongside His Majesty, the late king.\nWhat heady days those were!
MID_EV13_024_m01_013: Bona and I were young bucks back then. You were\nstill pretty small yourself, boss.
MID_EV13_024_m01_014: All of six years old. I tried to follow you, spear in\nhand, in order to do my part.
MID_EV13_024_m01_015: But Kumos seized me by the collar. If not for him,\nI would have seen combat that day.
MID_EV13_024_m01_016: Today I shall perform the great feats I was denied\nmy chance at before.
MID_EV13_024_m01_017: By the way, mark that man in the center. His face\nis hidden, but he strikes me as bloodthirsty.
MID_EV13_024_m01_018: Just so. Rarely have I seen a man so clearly bent\non violence.
MID_EV13_024_m01_019: It would not surprise me to learn he was the spirit\nof a Mosa warrior you killed.
MID_EV13_024_m01_020: What's this? Incredible... I've never seen it react\nthis strongly.
MID_EV13_024_m01_021: What is it reacting to? Should we be anticipating\nan especially powerful foe?
MID_EV13_024_m01_022: It certainly seems that way. There's no telling what\nthis brute's capable of.
MID_EV13_024_m01_023: Is checking your compass some sort of superstition,\nor are you being deliberately irritating?
MID_EV13_024_m01_024: This is no ordinary compass—this here's\nDhaba's Compass.
MID_EV13_024_m01_025: When it gets a reading, it's best to be wary.
MID_EV13_024_m01_026: And it's getting a strong reading off our friend\nthere—so we should be wary of him.
MID_EV13_024_m01_027: I needed only my own eyes to know he is dangerous,\nyou simpleton.
MID_EV13_024_m01_028: Of course. What I mean is this is telling me he's\neven more dangerous than he looks.
MID_EV13_024_m01_029: Just...be careful out there, Majesty. My plans rely\non us winning this.
MID_EV13_024_m01_030: If you are apprehensive, I volunteer to lead our clash\nwith the enemy. I'll be able to gauge his strength.
MID_EV13_024_m01_031: What are you implying?! I grow tired of your\ncondescension.
MID_EV13_024_m01_032: Remember what I told you? I am here to protect you.
MID_EV13_024_m01_033: Theodora, you and the people of Saramis are among\nthose selected for my protection.
MID_EV13_024_m01_034: It is within my power to keep you safe. There's no\nneed to feel ashamed.
MID_EV13_025_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_025_m01_001: Great work out there, you two. Excellent stuff.
MID_EV13_025_m01_002: That device of yours—what is that? It's incredible!\nWhat does it fire, some kind of magic lightning?
MID_EV13_025_m01_003: Can anyone use it? Including people who have no\nmagical ability? Can I take a closer look?
MID_EV13_025_m01_004: It's so compact too... Amazing. You know, I frequent\nthe Morfis area for business...
MID_EV13_025_m01_005: This is my first time seeing anything like this though.\nIt's an intriguing little device. Are you willing to sell?
MID_EV13_025_m01_006: I'd go as high as 30 thousand. That's well within our\nbudget, isn't it, Ursula?
MID_EV13_025_m01_007: That would be an acceptable expense.
MID_EV13_025_m01_008: Wait, hang on. Exactly how much money is that?
MID_EV13_025_m01_009: Next to one night of lodging, that sounds like...\nenough to buy just about anything!
MID_EV13_025_m01_041: Wait, hang on. Exactly how much money is that?
MID_EV13_025_m01_042: Next to one night of lodging, that sounds like...\nenough to buy just about anything!
MID_EV13_025_m01_010: I advise you not to sell to this man. I can offer\na fairer price of 50 thousand gold.
MID_EV13_025_m01_011: Oho! Well, if I'm being honest, what I'm really\ninterested in is that arm of yours, Majesty.
MID_EV13_025_m01_012: I collect Drake's treasures, you see. You might call\nit a hobby of mine.
MID_EV13_025_m01_013: Or you could call it charity work... Either way, that\narm of yours IS one of Drake's treasures, is it not?
MID_EV13_025_m01_014: I know nothing of Drake or his treasures. This arm\nwas a blessing from the warrior Mahadu.
MID_EV13_025_m01_015: Well, however you got it, what do you say? I'd pay\nas much as a million for the whole arm.
MID_EV13_025_m01_016: Talimun! A million? Surely not...
MID_EV13_025_m01_017: All of Drake's treasures—down to every fingernail\nand strand of hair—hold some amount of power.
MID_EV13_025_m01_018: Even a tiny sliver can cost 10 thousand or more.
MID_EV13_025_m01_019: Not that they're much use to anyone beyond rich old\nbastards trying to compensate for their lost youths...
MID_EV13_025_m01_020: But an entire ARM? No one's bought an entire\narm before. A million seems more than fair!
MID_EV13_025_m01_021: A million gold, you say? That much could support\n10 thousand frontline soldiers for two months.
MID_EV13_025_m01_022: It's a tempting sum, but Saramis is not so desperate\nfor funds.
MID_EV13_025_m01_023: Besides which, this arm is not easily removed. It is\nattached to me as if it were my own.
MID_EV13_025_m01_024: Perhaps you can claim it when I die, if you haven't\nforgotten entirely by then.
MID_EV13_025_m01_025: Really?! You've got a deal! I don't suppose I could get\nthat in writing, could I?
MID_EV13_025_m01_026: Saraminians do not write. A businessman like you\nmust know this.
MID_EV13_025_m01_027: Why are you here, anyway? What are you scheming?
MID_EV13_025_m01_028: You claim to collect Drake's treasures, but you have\nmoney enough to buy them. What is your true aim?
MID_EV13_025_m01_029: Why, to get the great Divine Sovereign to sell to me.\nSell me Dagda, I mean. The whole thing.
MID_EV13_025_m01_030: You want to buy the entirety of Dagda? What\nfevered nonsense is this?
MID_EV13_025_m01_031: I jest, of course. Just a joke, Majesty.
MID_EV13_025_m01_032: Hey, boss! They're on the move!
MID_EV13_025_m01_043: Hey, boss! They're on the move!
MID_EV13_025_m01_033: It appears I have some other business to attend to,\nso I'll take my leave. I hope we meet again.
MID_EV13_025_m01_034: Remember—any of you find one of Drake's treasures,\nyou bring it to Talimun. Alright? I pay well!
MID_EV13_025_m01_035: {SetColor=Gray}Drake's treasures...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_025_m01_036: So that's Talimun of the Vandahl Trading Company.\nHe is a crafty one.
MID_EV13_025_m01_037: Even if it was a jest...could you keep a straight face\nwhile boasting of buying Dagda itself?
MID_EV13_025_m01_038: Vandahl has unimaginable resources. He may not\nhave been speaking figuratively.
MID_EV13_025_m01_039: He would not have entered this tournament idly.\nBut his true intentions are impossible to know.
MID_EV13_025_m01_040: If we do not keep our wits about us, he may yet take\nus for all we are worth.
MID_EV13_026_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_026_m01_001: Wait. I wish to confirm something with you.\nIs it true that you are of the White Egg?
MID_EV13_026_m01_002: Do you happen to know Troy?
MID_EV13_026_m01_003: I am Anatolia of Kunlun, a Nuwa Mediator. As you\nsay, I am one of the People of the White Egg.
MID_EV13_026_m01_004: And I've been told I can find an ally by the name of\nTroy here in Dagda.
MID_EV13_026_m01_005: I never dreamed there were any surviving People of\nthe White Egg.
MID_EV13_026_m01_006: We've survived—through much challenge—in the\nforbidden land sequestered away by the temples.
MID_EV13_026_m01_007: However, my people are on the verge of extinction.\nI am fighting here to save everyone in my village.
MID_EV13_026_m01_008: I grasp now your identity and circumstances.\nYet I will never concede victory.
MID_EV13_026_m01_009: On my shoulders rests a wish that must be fulfilled\nfor the good of all my people.
MID_EV13_026_m01_010: If there is no room for concession, then we must give\nall we've got when the time comes.
MID_EV13_026_m01_011: This has all been too much for one day. Feels like my\nhead's gonna explode.
MID_EV13_026_m01_012: Anatolia, Talimun, and Bahr Vahn as well...
MID_EV13_026_m01_013: I had hoped to never meet his like again. Is this,\ntoo, a link in the chain of causality?
MID_EV13_026_m01_014: Something he said bothers me. He spoke of\nbecoming a "demon god in full."
MID_EV13_026_m01_015: Was it a mere figure of speech, or was he revealing\nsomething of this power's nature?
MID_EV13_026_m01_016: Bah. It matters little, so long as I have strength to\nwin this tournament.
MID_EV13_026_m01_017: {SetColor=Gray}Even if the curse does consume me.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_026_m01_018: {SetColor=Gray}Hm?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_026_m01_019: {SetColor=Gray}Another crack in the warding chain? This is\na bad omen.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_026_m01_020: {SetColor=Gray}I thought I'd have more time.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_026_m01_021: The match itself left me uneasy. His was a face I\nhoped never to see again.
MID_EV13_026_m01_022: It's been misfortune after misfortune since coming to\nDagsion. I am growing frustrated.
MID_EV13_026_m01_023: I will see if I can find any avenues for Your Majesty\nto relax.
MID_EV13_026_m01_024: Excuse me, but I heard an odd rumor and thought\nthat Your Majesty should know.
MID_EV13_026_m01_025: The sentries say that Bahr Vahn was carried away\nafter the match by persons unknown.
MID_EV13_026_m01_026: He may attack again if he recovers. We should\nbolster the guard at the guest quarters.
MID_EV13_026_m01_027: There is more, Your Majesty. Apparently, Talimun\nwas tailing the villain's caretakers.
MID_EV13_026_m01_028: Just what is that man scheming now?